  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "You can dump the stack & heap of the UdonVM by crashing it, but it would be more useful to just have a method that returns a string of the current state of the stack & heap of the UdonVM the program is running in. This is useful when debugging in certain scenarios when working with the Udon Assembly or if your debugging an Udon Compiler presenting unexpected behaviour.\n\nDump Ex:\n[<color=yellow>UdonBehaviour</color>] VRC.Udon.VM.UdonVMException: The VM encountered an error!\nException Message:\n  An exception occurred during EXTERN to 'SystemInt32.__op_Addition__SystemInt32_SystemInt32__SystemInt32'.\n  Cannot retrieve heap variable of type 'UInt32' as type 'Int32'\n----------------------\nProgram Counter was at: 30\n----------------------\nStack Dump:\n  0: 0x00000000\n  1: 0x00000003\n  2: 0x00000002\n----------------------\nHeap Dump:\n  0: 0\n  1: 0\n  2: 5\n  3: 5\n  4: SystemInt32.__op_Addition__SystemInt32_SystemInt32__SystemInt32\n\nDumped by passing 2 uints into a int addition operation which crashes the VM.",
